<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hispania</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Roman Iberia, Roman Hispania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hispania was the Roman name for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>, conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from 218 BCE until the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> in 19 BCE. It was divided first into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a> and Ulterior and later into Tarraconensis, Baetica and Lusitania. One of the most Romanised parts of the empire, it gave Rome the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> and Hadrian and fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanic-peoples">Germanic peoples</a> in the 5th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hispania.jpg" alt="Hispania" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HansenBCN · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conquista_Hispania.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
